### Module 2 — NLP Layer

Text processing and similarity computation — the intelligence layer.

#### [NEW] [nlp/text_cleaner.py](file:///c:/Users/laksh/Desktop/IntlQ/nlp/text_cleaner.py)
- `clean_text(text)` → lowercase, remove punctuation, strip HTML
- `remove_stopwords(tokens)` → NLTK stopword removal
- `lemmatize(tokens)` → WordNet lemmatizer
- `preprocess(text)` → full pipeline returning cleaned token list

#### [NEW] [nlp/similarity.py](file:///c:/Users/laksh/Desktop/IntlQ/nlp/similarity.py)
- `tfidf_similarity(answer, ideal_answer)` → TF-IDF vectorization + cosine similarity (scikit-learn)
- Returns a float `0.0–1.0`

#### [NEW] [nlp/keyword_matcher.py](file:///c:/Users/laksh/Desktop/IntlQ/nlp/keyword_matcher.py)
- `match_keywords(answer_tokens, expected_keywords)` → returns `{ matched: [...], missing: [...], coverage_score: float }`

---

### Module 3 — Core Engine

Business logic for running interviews and evaluating answers.

#### [NEW] [core/interview_engine.py](file:///c:/Users/laksh/Desktop/IntlQ/core/interview_engine.py)
- `get_questions(role_id, difficulty, count)` → loads from JSON, filters, returns randomized question set
- Tracks question order for session

#### [NEW] [core/answer_processor.py](file:///c:/Users/laksh/Desktop/IntlQ/core/answer_processor.py)
- `process_answer(raw_text)` → calls NLP pipeline, returns cleaned/tokenized answer
- Entry point before evaluation

#### [NEW] [core/evaluator.py](file:///c:/Users/laksh/Desktop/IntlQ/core/evaluator.py)
- `evaluate(question_id, processed_answer)` → orchestrates similarity + keyword matching
- Returns `{ similarity_score, keyword_coverage, matched_keywords, missing_keywords }`

#### [NEW] [core/scoring.py](file:///c:/Users/laksh/Desktop/IntlQ/core/scoring.py)
- `calculate_score(similarity, keyword_coverage, weights)` → weighted formula
- Default weights: 60% similarity, 40% keyword coverage
- Returns `{ total_score, grade, breakdown }`

#### [NEW] [core/feedback_engine.py](file:///c:/Users/laksh/Desktop/IntlQ/core/feedback_engine.py)
- `generate_feedback(eval_result, score_result)` → produces structured feedback
- Returns `{ strengths: [...], improvements: [...], tips: [...], overall_comment }`

